DOCUMENT();      
loadMacros("PGbasicmacros.pl",
           "PGchoicemacros.pl",
           "PGanswermacros.pl",

);
TEXT(beginproblem(), $BR,$BBOLD, "Change of Basis", $EBOLD, $BR,$BR);

# True false questions are a special case of a "select list"
# Make a new select list
$tf = new_select_list();
# $tf now "contains" the select list object.
# Insert some  questions and whether or not they are true.

$tf -> qa ( # each entry has to end with a comma
"If $SPACE$SPACE \(\displaystyle P = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & \phantom{-}2 & \phantom{-}3 \\ 1 & \phantom{-}2 & -3 \\ 1 & -2 & -3 \end{bmatrix}\), $SPACE$SPACE and $SPACE$SPACE \(B' = \{v_1,v_2,v_3\}\) $SPACE$SPACE is a basis of some abstract finite dimensional vector space \(V\), then \(P\) is the transition matrix from $SPACE$SPACE \(\displaystyle B = \{v_1+v_2+v_3,2v_1+2v_2-2v_3,3v_1-3v_2-3v_3\}\) $SPACE$SPACE to $SPACE$SPACE \(B'\).",
"T",
"Every transition matrix is invertible.",
"T",
"If \(B,B'\) are two bases of an abstract finite dimensional vector space \(V\) with the property that each vector in \(B'\) is a scalar multiple of some vector in \(B\), then the transition matrix from \(B'\) to \(B\) is diagonal.",
"F",
"Given bases \(B = \{ 1, x, x^2 \}\) and \(B' = \{ x^2, x, 1 \}\) of \(P_2\), the space of polynomials of degree 2 or less, the transition matrix from \(B\) to \(B'\) is the \(3\times 3\) identity matrix.",
"F",
"The transition matrix from one basis to another of \(M_4(\mathbb{R})\), the space of \(4 \times 4\) matrices with real entries, has size \(16 \times 16\).",
"T",
);   

# Choose five of the question and answer pairs at random.
$tf ->choose(5);

# Now print the text using $ml->print_q for the questions
# and $ml->print_a to print the answers.

BEGIN_TEXT
$PAR

Enter T or F depending on whether the statement is true or false.
(You must enter T or F -- True and False will not work.)

$PAR

\{ $tf-> print_q \}

$PAR

END_TEXT

# Enter the correct answers to be checked against the answers to the students.

install_problem_grader(~~&std_problem_grader);
# Since this is a true questions, we do not usually wish to tell students which
# parts of the matching question have been answered correctly and which are
# incorrect.  That is too easy.  To accomplish this we set the following flag to
# zero.
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

ANS(str_cmp( $tf->ra_correct_ans )   ) ;

ENDDOCUMENT();        # This should be the last executable line in the problem.
